  "live_records": {
    "q-85668": {
      "dom_id": "step-q85668",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "What is the sum of the series $-\\frac{\\pi }{3}+\\frac{(\\pi /3)^{3}}{3!}-\\frac{(\\pi /3)^{5}}{5!}+⋯+\\frac{(-1)^{n}(-\\pi /3)^{2n+1}}{(2n+1)!}+⋯\\,?$",
      "worked_solution": "We recognize that the series looks similar to the Maclaurin expansion for $f(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & =x-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3!}+\\frac{{x}^{5}}{5!}-⋯+\\frac{(-1)^{n}{x}^{2n+1}}{(2n+1)!}+⋯\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=-\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ into our Maclaurin expansion gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-\\frac{\\pi }{3}) & =(-\\frac{\\pi }{3})-\\frac{(-\\pi /3)^{3}}{3!}+\\frac{(-\\pi /3)^{5}}{5!}-\\frac{(-\\pi /3)^{7}}{7!}+⋯+\\frac{(-1)^{n}(-\\pi /3)^{2n+1}}{(2n+1)!}+⋯ \\\\ -\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} & =-\\frac{\\pi }{3}+\\frac{(\\pi /3)^{3}}{3!}-\\frac{(\\pi /3)^{5}}{5!}+\\frac{(\\pi /3)^{7}}{7!}-⋯+\\frac{(-1)^{n}(-\\pi /3)^{2n+1}}{(2n+1)!}+⋯\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the sum of the series is $-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
