    "q-103097": {
      "dom_id": "step-q103097",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "What is the sum of the series $\\frac{2\\pi }{3}-\\frac{(2\\pi /3)^{3}}{3!}+\\frac{(2\\pi /3)^{5}}{5!}-⋯+\\frac{(-1)^{n}(2\\pi /3)^{2n+1}}{(2n+1)!}+⋯\\,?$",
      "worked_solution": "We recognize that the series looks similar to the Maclaurin expansion for $f(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & =x-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3!}+\\frac{{x}^{5}}{5!}-⋯+\\frac{(-1)^{n}{x}^{2n+1}}{(2n+1)!}+⋯\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\frac{2\\pi }{3}$ into our Maclaurin expansion gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{2\\pi }{3}) & =\\frac{2\\pi }{3}-\\frac{(2\\pi /3)^{3}}{3!}+\\frac{(2\\pi /3)^{5}}{5!}-\\frac{(2\\pi /3)^{7}}{7!}+⋯+\\frac{(-1)^{n}(2\\pi /3)^{2n+1}}{(2n+1)!}+⋯ \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} & =\\frac{2\\pi }{3}-\\frac{(2\\pi /3)^{3}}{3!}+\\frac{(2\\pi /3)^{5}}{5!}-\\frac{(2\\pi /3)^{7}}{7!}+⋯+\\frac{(-1)^{n}(2\\pi /3)^{2n+1}}{(2n+1)!}+⋯\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the sum of the series is $\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
