    "q-103105": {
      "dom_id": "step-q103105",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "What is the sum of the series $-\\frac{3}{2}+\\frac{27}{8\\cdot 3!}-\\frac{243}{32\\cdot 5!}+⋯+\\frac{(-1)^{n}(-3)^{2n+1}}{{2}^{2n+1}(2n+1)!}+⋯\\,?$",
      "worked_solution": "We recognize that the series looks similar to the Maclaurin expansion for $f(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & =x-\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3!}+\\frac{{x}^{5}}{5!}-⋯+\\frac{(-1)^{n}{x}^{2n+1}}{(2n+1)!}+⋯\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=-\\frac{3}{2}$ into our Maclaurin expansion gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-\\frac{3}{2}) & =(-\\frac{3}{2})-\\frac{(-3/2)^{3}}{3!}+\\frac{(-3/2)^{5}}{5!}-⋯+\\frac{(-1)^{n}(-3/2)^{2n+1}}{(2n+1)!}+⋯ \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3}{2}) & =-\\frac{3}{2}+\\frac{{3}^{3}}{{2}^{3}\\cdot 3!}-\\frac{{3}^{5}}{{2}^{5}\\cdot 5!}+⋯+\\frac{(-1)^{n}(-3)^{2n+1}}{{2}^{2n+1}(2n+1)!}+⋯ \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3}{2}) & =-\\frac{3}{2}+\\frac{27}{8\\cdot 3!}-\\frac{243}{32\\cdot 5!}+⋯+\\frac{(-1)^{n}(-3)^{2n+1}}{{2}^{2n+1}(2n+1)!}+⋯\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the sum of the series is $-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3}{2}).$",
